  message: "RE-MEASURED after WI-ripas (pre-registered in ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/mojaz_remeasure_09222026/PREREG.md before any number existed). pretix, --include-non-production-sources, analyzer dev 4610d2d693 pinned, 0022's classifier and rubric.\n\nCONTROL: 0022's 119 sampled keys, re-classified on 0022's ledger, reproduce 0022's stored verdicts 119/119. The harness is the instrument.\n\nPOPULATION: 613 -> 1,084 situations (tree growth since 0022's 73a5fdb02f).\nLABEL MIX (rows): structural 367/637 (58%) -> 78/1,124 (7%). ddg_mixed/not_attempted 969 (86%). PREDICTION HELD: the structural share collapsed.\n\nPRECISION, not predicted in either direction:\n  0022 ambient                 23/95  = 24.2%  [16.7 .. 33.7]\n  paired (same 119 keys, now)  27/95  = 28.4%\n  fresh seeded sample (120)    28/102 = 27.5%\nUNCHANGED WITHIN NOISE, as the mechanism predicts: relabelling removes no flow, and a walk that is not attempted cannot remove one. So the row's subject, a ~76% false-positive arm, is NOT fixed by WI-ripas. It is ~72% now. WI-ripas cured the CAUSE the row asked about (structural by construction); it did not cure the FP rate.\n\nWHERE THE FALSE POSITIVES ARE (fresh sample, verdict x first blocker):\n  sink_before_source   22 FP /  0 TP  (+6 vacuous)   <- the row's own \"create earlier, assert on get later\" shape\n  source_not_tracked   22 FP / 13 TP\n  cross_function       22 FP / 12 TP\nRefuting sink_before_source (hops=0) would take this arm from 27.5% to 35.0% with no sampled TP lost. With n=22 and 0 TP, the 95% upper bound on the TP share is ~15%. It is a REMOVAL rule, and ADR-0052 makes refutation confirm-only, so this needs an owner ruling. A loop-carried value is the soundness exception to handle.\n\nStatus stays todo_hard: the condition in the title still holds."  # 56e3
